WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.630
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.900 --> 00:02.570
Can I meet her?

3
00:02.570 --> 00:06.310
Please. I want to move on.

4
00:06.310 --> 00:09.110
How about you come over, and we brainstorm a plan?

5
00:09.110 --> 00:10.830
No one else is home today.

6
00:10.830 --> 00:14.880
Alone, in Watarai's house.

7
00:14.880 --> 00:17.530
Will I really be okay?

8
00:25.270 --> 00:27.180
All right.

9
00:31.520 --> 00:34.430
Should we get to it?

10
00:38.400 --> 00:39.780
Huh?

11
00:39.780 --> 00:42.440
The brainstorming.

12
00:42.440 --> 00:44.940
Right. The brainstorming.

13
00:44.940 --> 00:46.510
Yeah.

14
00:46.510 --> 00:51.300
Here's one idea.

15
00:51.300 --> 00:57.200
I could have a girl pretend to be my girlfriend. What do you think?

16
00:58.770 --> 01:04.310
Would that only entail visiting your ex together?

17
01:05.300 --> 01:08.320
- What do you mean? - Well...

18
01:08.320 --> 01:11.000
Would you two need to hold hands?

19
01:11.000 --> 01:13.720
- Or kiss? - Of course not.

20
01:14.840 --> 01:18.790
But...

21
01:21.180 --> 01:24.060
I guess I'd need to be close to her.

22
01:24.060 --> 01:27.660
Sorry. You wouldn't like that, right?

23
01:27.660 --> 01:33.210
Yeah. In that case, I'd rather go see your ex myself.

24
01:33.210 --> 01:34.790
Really?

25
01:35.450 --> 01:37.810
You wouldn't mind meeting her?

26
01:37.810 --> 01:39.780
Yeah.

27
01:39.780 --> 01:42.890
She might not believe us though.

28
01:42.890 --> 01:45.660
Maybe we should look the part of a couple?

29
01:45.660 --> 01:48.740
What does that even mean?

30
01:49.440 --> 01:50.770
Good question.

31
01:50.770 --> 01:52.680
Matching outfits?

32
01:55.220 --> 01:57.630
Matching outfits...

33
01:59.810 --> 02:02.430
That'd make her even more suspicious of us.

34
02:02.430 --> 02:04.260
Yeah, probably.

35
02:05.510 --> 02:09.170
How else can we seem more like a couple?

36
02:09.170 --> 02:11.790
"Things couples do".

37
02:11.790 --> 02:14.080
[What people do once they're dating?]

38
02:18.280 --> 02:20.520
[Displays of affection (kissing, sex, etc.)]

39
02:26.300 --> 02:29.040
- Did you find something? - No.

40
02:29.040 --> 02:31.590
Really?

41
02:31.590 --> 02:33.370
What?

42
02:33.370 --> 02:35.540
- You're hiding something. - No.

43
02:35.540 --> 02:37.220
- Let me see. - No.

44
02:37.220 --> 02:40.310
- Why not? - No, well...

45
02:44.260 --> 02:46.040
Hey!

46
02:50.720 --> 02:52.160
What?

47
02:52.160 --> 02:56.400
No, it just popped up! I wasn't...

48
03:02.400 --> 03:04.140
Hioki.

49
03:05.070 --> 03:07.600
You're interested in stuff like that?

50
03:07.600 --> 03:09.080
Huh?

51
03:10.440 --> 03:15.670
Have you thought about doing it with me?

52
03:19.130 --> 03:22.350
Have you?

53
03:23.770 --> 03:25.520
I...

54
03:26.450 --> 03:28.150
I have.

55
03:30.860 --> 03:33.350
What about you, Hioki?

56
03:33.350 --> 03:34.890
Do you not want to?

57
03:38.160 --> 03:40.250
Should I not touch you?

58
03:45.490 --> 03:47.570
I'm not against it...

59
05:07.260 --> 05:08.690
Wait.

60
05:08.690 --> 05:10.760
Someone's home.

61
05:10.760 --> 05:13.970
Huh? Your mom?

62
05:16.170 --> 05:18.370
No, these steps...

63
05:18.370 --> 05:19.920
This is probably...

64
05:23.920 --> 05:26.480
Tsukasa, I'm home!

65
06:30.650 --> 06:32.870
I jumped four layers of a vaulting horse today! [Battle Plan]

66
06:32.870 --> 06:34.330
Four layers? That's amazing!

67
06:34.330 --> 06:35.510
Right?

68
06:35.510 --> 06:37.780
I also made a fish during arts and crafts!

69
06:37.780 --> 06:40.110
I named it the Ultimate Shark.

70
06:40.110 --> 06:42.500
Ultimate Shark? Sounds tough.

71
06:42.500 --> 06:45.240
Yeah, he's super tough!

72
06:45.240 --> 06:46.940
- Is that so? -I'll show you!

73
06:46.940 --> 06:48.970
- Really? - Tsumugi.

74
06:48.970 --> 06:51.690
- Homework first. - Later!

75
06:54.460 --> 06:56.540
Sorry.

76
06:56.540 --> 07:00.560
Tsumugi was supposed to be with Mom today,

77
07:00.560 --> 07:02.110
but she got called into work.

78
07:02.110 --> 07:04.970
Don't worry about it.

79
07:04.970 --> 07:07.720
I got us pudding, so let's have some later.

80
07:07.720 --> 07:09.390
Really? Thanks!

81
07:09.390 --> 07:13.070
Your younger brother is so cute. You said he was in second grade?

82
07:13.070 --> 07:14.570
Yeah.

83
07:18.440 --> 07:23.070
We'll continue the rest later.

84
07:23.070 --> 07:24.970
Continue?

85
07:30.550 --> 07:32.580
Our brainstorming.

86
07:33.700 --> 07:35.150
Oh.

87
07:38.850 --> 07:42.740
Sorry. I almost lost control earlier.

88
07:44.530 --> 07:47.730
As for our other activity,

89
07:47.730 --> 07:51.720
let's pick things up when we're adults, okay?

90
07:58.780 --> 08:01.390
Asahi, let's play!

91
08:01.390 --> 08:03.110
What happened to your Ultimate Shark?

92
08:03.110 --> 08:04.460
I forgot.

93
08:04.460 --> 08:06.140
- I see. - Let's play!

94
08:06.140 --> 08:07.710
- Sure. - Tsumugi.

95
08:07.710 --> 08:09.180
No sitting there.

96
08:09.180 --> 08:10.820
- Why not? - Because.

97
08:10.820 --> 08:13.550
No. I wanna sit on Asahi's lap.

98
08:13.550 --> 08:15.460
No whining.

99
08:15.460 --> 08:16.660
- Get off. - Don't wanna!

100
08:16.660 --> 08:18.560
Sit here.

101
08:18.560 --> 08:21.130
Why? Am I not allowed?

102
08:21.130 --> 08:22.330
No, you can sit here.

103
08:22.330 --> 08:24.750
Yay!

104
08:24.750 --> 08:26.040
No fair.

105
08:26.040 --> 08:27.950
Then Hioki will sit on my lap.

106
08:27.950 --> 08:29.770
Why?

107
08:29.770 --> 08:32.130
Asahi, what should we play first?

108
08:32.130 --> 08:35.450
Good question.

109
08:35.450 --> 08:37.260
- How about... - This one?

110
08:37.260 --> 08:39.930
I'm not very good at that game...

111
08:45.170 --> 08:46.560
Fall, fall!

112
08:46.560 --> 08:48.110
Hold on.

113
08:48.110 --> 08:50.410
- Uh oh. - You sure about that one?

114
08:50.410 --> 08:52.850
Oh no!

115
08:52.850 --> 08:55.210
- High five, Tsumugi! - Asahi gets his forehead flicked!

116
08:55.210 --> 08:57.460
This sucks...

117
08:57.460 --> 08:59.900
Have a staring contest,

118
08:59.900 --> 09:02.280
whoever laughs loses,

119
09:02.280 --> 09:05.120
ready, and go!

120
09:08.280 --> 09:10.370
- You're strong! - You lose.

121
09:10.370 --> 09:11.670
Way too strong.

122
09:11.670 --> 09:14.460
Now, play against Tsukasa.

123
09:14.460 --> 09:15.780
Huh?

124
09:15.780 --> 09:18.010
- Me? - Yeah!

125
09:18.010 --> 09:20.890
Have a staring contest,

126
09:20.890 --> 09:24.630
whoever laughs...

127
09:24.630 --> 09:25.900
You two are so weak.

128
09:25.900 --> 09:27.420
It's because Hioki was embarrassed!

129
09:27.420 --> 09:29.770
I wasn't embarrassed.

130
09:29.770 --> 09:31.780
Voilà.

131
09:31.780 --> 09:34.060
- Looks yummy! - Yeah.

132
09:34.060 --> 09:35.420
Did you wash your hands, Tsumugi?

133
09:35.420 --> 09:37.270
Yup.

134
09:37.270 --> 09:39.140
Which one do I choose...

135
09:39.140 --> 09:40.420
Hold on.

136
09:40.420 --> 09:42.920
The guest chooses first.

137
09:42.920 --> 09:45.500
- Okay. - Go ahead, Hioki.

138
09:45.500 --> 09:48.450
Right, the spoons. Be right back.

139
09:53.710 --> 09:56.110
You can choose first.

140
09:56.110 --> 09:58.950
- Really? - Yeah. What's your pick?

141
09:58.950 --> 10:00.470
- Chocolate! - Good choice.

142
10:00.470 --> 10:02.210
Here you go.

143
10:02.210 --> 10:04.990
Thank you!

144
10:04.990 --> 10:07.320
- Hioki... - Why not?

145
10:07.320 --> 10:09.480
- Right? - Right!

146
10:10.840 --> 10:12.410
Which one do you want, Watarai?

147
10:12.410 --> 10:14.240
Tsukasa.

148
10:14.240 --> 10:17.080
- Huh? - His name is Tsukasa.

149
10:21.890 --> 10:23.650
You heard him.

150
10:27.800 --> 10:30.200
Which one do you want, Tsukasa?

151
10:33.460 --> 10:36.060
I'm fine with any of them.

152
10:36.060 --> 10:38.210
You choose first, Asahi.

153
10:42.990 --> 10:45.960
Asahi? You're getting embarrassed.

154
10:45.960 --> 10:48.500
I'll have the caramel one.

155
11:02.940 --> 11:04.620
- Did he fall asleep? - Yeah.

156
11:07.480 --> 11:09.310
I'll help.

157
11:09.310 --> 11:11.000
Thanks.

158
11:11.820 --> 11:15.770
Sorry you had to entertain Tsumugi.

159
11:15.770 --> 11:18.380
I didn't mind. I had fun.

160
11:18.380 --> 11:21.310
And I got to see you be a big brother.

161
11:21.310 --> 11:25.320
I'm more surprised Tsumugi isn't shy with strangers.

162
11:25.320 --> 11:28.590
He usually is.

163
11:29.610 --> 11:31.550
You're the exception.

164
11:31.550 --> 11:33.120
Really?

165
11:33.120 --> 11:38.360
Yeah. It's probably because I talk about you often.

166
11:39.270 --> 11:42.740
Did you mention we were dating?

167
11:42.740 --> 11:44.680
No.

168
11:44.680 --> 11:48.620
I just talk about stuff that happens at school.

169
11:48.620 --> 11:51.250
And I bring up our outings sometimes.

170
11:54.330 --> 11:58.140
Should I tell my family about us?

171
11:58.140 --> 11:59.800
No, it's fine.

172
12:00.460 --> 12:03.930
Besides, I haven't told my family either.

173
12:13.430 --> 12:15.550
Hioki.

174
12:15.550 --> 12:17.630
Should we call it off?

175
12:17.630 --> 12:19.840
You meeting Suzu, I mean.

176
12:19.840 --> 12:21.470
Huh?

177
12:21.470 --> 12:27.180
I mean, if we haven't even told our parents,

178
12:27.180 --> 12:30.410
why do we need to tell Suzu?

179
12:44.770 --> 12:47.580
We haven't told our parents.

180
13:09.700 --> 13:13.150
He makes a fair point.

181
13:13.150 --> 13:17.560
I mean the only people who know we're dating are...

182
13:20.610 --> 13:22.730
You're finally here! Hurry.

183
13:22.730 --> 13:25.270
- Huh? - Hurry, hurry!

184
13:25.270 --> 13:27.480
I can walk alone.

185
13:27.480 --> 13:29.030
Morning. What's up?

186
13:29.030 --> 13:31.170
So, tell us.

187
13:31.170 --> 13:33.710
What happened with Watarai's ex?

188
13:33.710 --> 13:35.880
Oh, right.

189
13:35.880 --> 13:38.550
Was everything okay? Were you two able to talk?

190
13:38.550 --> 13:41.300
I was so curious, I could only sleep at night!

191
13:41.300 --> 13:44.720
Hold on. Where do I even start?

192
13:44.720 --> 13:46.830
- Take it slow. - No, tell us, now!

193
13:46.830 --> 13:48.530
Morning.

194
13:49.630 --> 13:51.470
What're you guys doing?

195
13:59.840 --> 14:03.380
Huh? Hioki will go meet your ex?

196
14:04.720 --> 14:06.720
Why?

197
14:06.720 --> 14:10.360
Definitely not the turn of events I expected.

198
14:10.360 --> 14:12.930
I'm just glad he wasn't cheating on Hioki.

199
14:12.930 --> 14:16.290
Huh? I would never do that.

200
14:16.290 --> 14:17.860
Sorry.

201
14:17.860 --> 14:22.640
So, right now, we're trying to figure out our next step.

202
14:22.640 --> 14:26.700
What do you three think about me meeting her?

203
14:27.960 --> 14:30.010
That's a bit...

204
14:30.010 --> 14:32.490
Yeah, sounds like a tall ask.

205
14:32.490 --> 14:34.050
I mean, how will you prove it?

206
14:34.050 --> 14:36.760
I plan to tell her the truth.

207
14:37.540 --> 14:41.180
Do you need to tell her everything though?

208
14:41.180 --> 14:43.570
Lying isn't always a bad option.

209
14:44.910 --> 14:47.520
Maybe we can ask a girl to pretend to be Watarai's girlfriend?

210
14:47.520 --> 14:48.660
That's a good idea!

211
14:48.660 --> 14:50.750
No can do.

212
14:50.750 --> 14:52.350
Why not?

213
14:53.040 --> 14:56.430
Because I wouldn't like it.

214
14:56.430 --> 14:58.030
It'd only be for a day.

215
14:58.030 --> 14:59.540
That's a day too long.

216
14:59.540 --> 15:01.200
I see.

217
15:01.200 --> 15:05.150
Then maybe telling the truth is their best option.

218
15:05.150 --> 15:06.750
About that.

219
15:08.040 --> 15:10.100
Could I ask you three a question?

220
15:12.290 --> 15:16.370
How did you guys first react

221
15:16.370 --> 15:18.210
when you heard about us?

222
15:22.430 --> 15:28.020
If I'm being completely honest, my gut reaction was, "For real?"

223
15:28.020 --> 15:32.210
But guys can become close friends.

224
15:32.210 --> 15:37.220
So, if I take it as an extension of that, it doesn't confuse me anymore.

225
15:37.220 --> 15:40.050
Personally, I get how you feel.

226
15:40.050 --> 15:43.830
Maybe not the romantic aspect of it,

227
15:43.830 --> 15:47.630
but it is easier to be around guys.

228
15:53.650 --> 15:56.600
It's not my life, so it's no big deal to me.

229
15:56.600 --> 15:58.170
Quit trying to act cool.

230
15:58.170 --> 15:59.350
What?

231
15:59.350 --> 16:03.400
Yeah, you're the one who's always so worried about these two.

232
16:03.400 --> 16:04.510
I am not.

233
16:04.510 --> 16:05.790
You totally are.

234
16:05.790 --> 16:08.810
- I mean, during study camp... - That's enough.

235
16:08.810 --> 16:10.230
Yeah, you were asking all about them.

236
16:10.230 --> 16:12.170
Sorry, forget it.

237
16:12.170 --> 16:14.260
Don't say any more.

238
16:14.260 --> 16:15.550
But you were all like,

239
16:15.550 --> 16:18.700
"Where'd Hioki and Watarai go?"

240
16:20.760 --> 16:22.750
Watarai.

241
16:22.750 --> 16:26.280
I also had a question for you.

242
16:26.280 --> 16:29.340
Sure. What is it?

243
16:31.640 --> 16:33.830
I wanted to ask about Suzu.

244
16:34.850 --> 16:40.550
Can you tell me what your relationship with her was like?

245
16:41.910 --> 16:43.430
Okay.

246
16:47.440 --> 16:49.850
We began dating in the winter.

247
16:49.850 --> 16:52.110
It was our second year of middle school

248
16:53.150 --> 16:56.240
I had been classmates with Suzu since our first year.

249
16:57.270 --> 17:02.890
My impression of her was that she was a strong, outgoing girl. Until...

250
17:02.890 --> 17:05.940
I like you.

251
17:07.480 --> 17:09.870
Would you...

252
17:11.680 --> 17:14.360
go out with me, please?

253
17:15.280 --> 17:19.170
[To Watarai]

254
17:19.170 --> 17:23.420
I'd never seen her so nervous before.

255
17:24.310 --> 17:25.790
Sure.

256
17:28.820 --> 17:33.410
But we were only middle schoolers.

257
17:34.220 --> 17:39.020
A walk home or around town were as far as our "dates" went.

258
17:39.970 --> 17:44.100
It really felt like our relationship was an extension of our friendship.

259
17:44.100 --> 17:45.710
But then...

260
17:49.820 --> 17:52.910
When we became high schoolers, Suzu started an Instagram.

261
17:52.910 --> 17:54.380
Here you go.

262
17:55.860 --> 17:57.630
Tsukasa, look!

263
17:57.630 --> 18:01.460
Everyone loves the earrings you gave me.

264
18:01.460 --> 18:02.900
They do?

265
18:02.900 --> 18:05.180
I see.

266
18:05.180 --> 18:08.870
A hot, sweet, gentleman of a boyfriend.

267
18:08.870 --> 18:11.210
Everyone is so jealous!

268
18:11.210 --> 18:14.860
Even when we spent time together, she'd be glued to her phone.

269
18:16.050 --> 18:19.200
That's when I realized she didn't like me, the person,

270
18:19.200 --> 18:22.270
but the person she became when she was with me.

271
18:22.270 --> 18:27.380
That's why I asked to break up with her the summer of our first year in high school.

272
18:28.130 --> 18:32.230
If you asked if I ever loved Suzu at all,

273
18:33.350 --> 18:36.410
honestly, I don't know.

274
18:36.410 --> 18:38.980
I tried to like her.

275
18:42.640 --> 18:49.820
But you're the first person I really fell in love with.

276
18:49.820 --> 18:51.270
Huh?

277
18:51.920 --> 18:53.920
I never told you?

278
18:55.500 --> 19:00.590
You're the only person I've ever loved so deeply.

279
19:02.110 --> 19:04.330
Just me?

280
19:04.330 --> 19:05.820
Yeah.

281
19:06.980 --> 19:09.120
You're the only one I ever fell for.

282
19:09.120 --> 19:12.210
The only one I chased after.

283
19:14.480 --> 19:16.850
The only one I get jealous over.

284
19:18.240 --> 19:20.940
The only one who makes me go crazy.

285
19:20.940 --> 19:23.680
It's only ever you.

286
19:23.680 --> 19:26.600
Hioki.

287
19:26.600 --> 19:28.420
You're my first crush.

288
19:42.830 --> 19:46.120
I'll go meet Suzu after all.

289
19:48.300 --> 19:49.780
Huh?

290
19:52.040 --> 19:53.630
Really?

291
19:53.630 --> 19:55.140
Yeah.

292
19:55.140 --> 19:58.430
I don't know if she'll believe us,

293
19:58.430 --> 20:00.240
but I think it'll work out.

294
20:00.240 --> 20:02.770
I mean, even Tsumugi could tell.

295
20:03.500 --> 20:04.890
Tsumugi?

296
20:04.890 --> 20:06.430
Yeah.

297
20:08.210 --> 20:11.260
Asahi?

298
20:11.260 --> 20:16.070
Tsukasa really likes you, doesn't he?

299
20:17.950 --> 20:21.060
Yeah. He really does.

300
20:22.960 --> 20:24.850
What about you, Asahi?

301
20:25.770 --> 20:29.130
You like him too, don't you?

302
20:31.820 --> 20:33.460
Yeah.

303
20:36.130 --> 20:38.850
I...

304
20:38.850 --> 20:40.750
I like him, too.

305
20:53.100 --> 20:57.430
Besides, even if we can't prove ourselves,

306
20:58.470 --> 21:02.640
I want to be the one at your side.

307
21:02.640 --> 21:04.790
Since, you know...

308
21:05.770 --> 21:07.760
I am your boyfriend and all.

309
21:20.530 --> 21:23.170
I just had a great idea.

310
21:23.170 --> 21:24.930
Come with me.

311
21:33.340 --> 21:34.600
Will this prove anything?

312
21:34.600 --> 21:36.210
Yeah. Good idea, right?

313
21:36.210 --> 21:37.530
I don't know...

314
21:37.530 --> 21:39.030
Let's just take one.

315
21:39.030 --> 21:40.200
[Take picture]

316
21:43.320 --> 21:45.190
Smile, smile!

317
21:45.190 --> 21:47.540
- Again. - Okay.

318
21:50.290 --> 21:51.680
It's a tight fit in here.

319
21:51.680 --> 21:53.330
No complaining.

320
21:53.330 --> 21:55.130
- Can I get a kiss shot? - No.

321
21:55.130 --> 21:57.580
- Why not? - Because.

322
22:01.870 --> 22:05.840
[RollerCoast]

323
22:14.110 --> 22:16.270
Nervous?

324
22:16.270 --> 22:19.410
No. I'm fine.

325
22:22.130 --> 22:24.020
Okay.

326
22:56.250 --> 23:00.120
